title: Saving a script while playing
intro: A script saved while the game plays starts the game over with the new version, clean, as a fresh Play would.
project: Platformer | Greeting Peaks

chapter: A script that spawns at Start | One sign
say: This script puts a sign up over its entity when the game starts.
write: Scripts/Greeter.cs | script-reload-while-playing/Greeter.cs
code: Assets/Scripts/Greeter.cs | Greeter.cs
hidecode
create: Empty
rename: Greeter
add: Greeter
play
wait: 1
expectcount: Greeting = 1
explain: game | One sign | The game starts, and the sign goes up once.

chapter: Change it mid-playtest | The game starts over
say: Now the script changes while the game plays, the way you'd tweak it mid-playtest.
write: Scripts/Greeter.cs | script-reload-while-playing/Greeter2.cs
wait: 1
expectcount: Greeting = 1
explain: game | Started over | The game started again from the scene as it was when you pressed Play, running the new version. Still one sign, with the new greeting, and nothing half old and half new.
say: Swapping the scripts into the game as it stood would have started each one again, putting up a second sign, without what each had kept in its own fields. Starting over is the same clean game a fresh Play gives.
stop
